The public function `stream_totals(records)` consumes an iterable of `(category, amount)` tuples and returns a new list of `(category, total)` tuples. Categories are non-empty strings, amounts are finite `int` or `float` values excluding booleans, and result order follows each category's first appearance. Empty input returns `[]`.

The function must process records one at a time with auxiliary storage proportional only to the number of distinct categories. It must not materialize or pre-consume the record stream. On a malformed record, raise `TypeError` or `ValueError` immediately without requesting a later record. Strings and bytes are invalid outer iterables; each record must be exactly a tuple of length two. Do not mutate or retain record aliases.

